          "level": 2,
          "content": "E X E R C I S E S"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.132,
            0.539,
            0.153
          ],
          "content": "**1. Which of the following is a plant hormone?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.153,
            0.28,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": "**(a) Insulin**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.172,
            0.296,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Thyroxin**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.193,
            0.303,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "**(c) Oestrogen**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.213,
            0.304,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": "**(d) Cytokinin.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.232,
            0.521,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "**2. The gap between two neurons is called a**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.252,
            0.29,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": "**(a) dendrite.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.272,
            0.289,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": "**(b) synapse.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.293,
            0.263,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": "**(c) axon.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.312,
            0.288,
            0.332
          ],
          "content": "**(d) impulse.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.331,
            0.407,
            0.351
          ],
          "content": "**3. The brain is responsible for**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.352,
            0.293,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": "**(a) thinking.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.371,
            0.433,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": "**(b) regulating the heart beat.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.392,
            0.387,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": "**(c) balancing the body.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.411,
            0.349,
            0.43
          ],
          "content": "**(d) all of the above.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.43,
            0.87,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": "**4. What is the function of receptors in our body? Think of situations where receptors do not work properly. What problems are likely to arise?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.467,
            0.659,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": "**5. Draw the structure of a neuron and explain its function.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.487,
            0.525,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": "**6. How does phototropism occur in plants?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.506,
            0.719,
            0.527
          ],
          "content": "**7. Which signals will get disrupted in case of a spinal cord injury?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.527,
            0.6,
            0.546
          ],
          "content": "**8. How does chemical coordination occur in plants?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.546,
            0.812,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": "**9. What is the need for a system of control and coordination in an organism?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.566,
            0.804,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": "**10. How are involuntary actions and reflex actions different from each other?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.586,
            0.87,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": "**11. Compare and contrast nervous and hormonal mechanisms for control and coordination in animals.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.621,
            0.87,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "**12. What is the difference between the manner in which movement takes place in a sensitive plant and the movement in our legs?**"
